 Nuclear reaction model code EMPIRE-3.2.3 Malta                   6725 1451
 (SVN rev. 4867 )                                                 6725 1451
 by M.W.Herman et al [EMP,EMP-man].                               6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
 EMPIRE dimensions (dimension.h):                                 6725 1451
  NDNUC= 150  NDEXCLUS= 20  NDEX= 201  NDLW= 100                  6725 1451
  LEVCC= 40  NDLV= 40  NDBR= 40  NDMSCS= 4                        6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                6725 1451
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               6725 1451
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
 This code integrates into a single system a number               6725 1451
 of important modules and features:                               6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 6725 1451
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      6725 1451
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  6725 1451
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                6725 1451
   and coworkers                                                  6725 1451
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    6725 1451
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          6725 1451
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 6725 1451
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                6725 1451
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       6725 1451
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      6725 1451
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 6725 1451
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                6725 1451
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               6725 1451
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                6725 1451
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   6725 1451
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                6725 1451
   discrete transitions                                           6725 1451
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                6725 1451
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                6725 1451
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               6725 1451
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 6725 1451
   library [RIPL]                                                 6725 1451
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              6725 1451
   EXFOR library                                                  6725 1451
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     6725 1451
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 6725 1451
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                6725 1451
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      6725 1451
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   6725 1451
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      6725 1451
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   6725 1451
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  6725 1451
 - generating covariances                                         6725 1451
 - Support for NJOY                                               6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
                                                                  6725 1451
